+## Native code editor
+
+`<input>` and `<textarea>` accept `runs` with UTF-16 `start`/`end` ranges and
+the same color, font, decoration and wash fields as `<rich-text>`. Later
+overlapping runs override earlier style fields. Update runs alongside the
+controlled `value`; native edits and undo remain immediate.
+
+`highlights` accepts `{start, end, color, active?, activeColor?}` ranges.
+`gutter={{color, activeColor?, width?, gap?, fontSize?}}` paints logical line
+numbers once per line, including when that line wraps. Width defaults to 42px
+and gap to 12px. `wrap={false}` enables horizontal scrolling; the default is
+soft wrapping. Read-only editors retain selection and copying but hide the
+editing caret.
+`secure={true}` masks display and accessibility text, disables copying, and
+retains real Unicode/UTF-16 editing offsets. Controlled change events still
+contain the real value; applications must not log them.
+
+`renderer.inputRevealRange(id, start, end)` reveals a UTF-16 range without
+changing selection. `renderer.inputScrollTo(id, x, y)` uses clamped pixel
+offsets. Existing `inputSetSelection` and `inputReplaceSelection` remain
+independent operations.
+
+Native editors emit key-down events in capture phase, before editor actions.
+JS callbacks cannot cancel native defaults retroactively. Use
+`interceptedKeys={["up", "down", "tab", "ctrl-v"]}` to intercept exact GPUI
+chords synchronously while still receiving `onKeyDown`; update the array
+when an autocomplete popup opens/closes. With `onSubmit`, Enter and
+Ctrl/Cmd+Enter submit (including `key` and `modifiers` in the payload), while
+Shift+Enter inserts a newline.
+
+Desktop renderers expose `windowBounds()` with the normal rectangle,
+maximized/fullscreen flags, and optional stable `displayId`, plus `closeWindow()`.
+Initialization accepts `x`, `y`, `maximized`, and `displayId` in addition to
+width/height. A missing saved display reanchors to the primary display;
+the origin is clamped to keep at least 160px of titlebar width and 22px of
+height visible. Placement remains compositor-controlled; there is no runtime
+window-position setter.
+
+`readClipboardPaths()` returns local paths from the desktop clipboard, or null.
+Container surfaces and editors support `onFileDragEnter`, `onFileDragLeave`,
+and `onFileDragMove` with `{x,y,paths,hovered}` payloads. Native OS cancellation
+and exit clear hover as well as movement outside the element. `onFileDrop`
+remains the drop/submit boundary.
+
